  :adr/status "accepted (implemented, landed to kotoba-lang/swift main)"
  :adr/date "2026-07-14"
  :adr/deciders ["Jun Kawasaki"]
  :adr/authoritative true
  :adr/authoritative_for ["kotoba-lang/swift upgraded from EDN-placeholder MT/ISO 20022 records to real, spec-verified wire format: MT103/MT202 real {1:}{2:}{3:}{4:}{5:} SWIFT FIN brace-block wire generation+lossless parsing, pain.001.001.09/pacs.008.001.08 real generated+parsed XML via kotoba-lang/xml"
                          "scope fence: MT103/MT202 only out of full SWIFT MT catalogue; pain.001.001.09/pacs.008.001.08 only out of full ISO 20022 catalogue; no SWIFT checksum algorithm; no XSD validation; no SWIFTNet/bank connection ever from this codebase (licensed FI required, out of scope)"
                          "every field tag / format constraint / element name independently verified against public sources before encoding (SWIFT field-tag references, MT developer guide, raw MT103 example, T26 usage rule, ISO 20022 implementation guides, ChargeBearerType1Code code list) -- full citations in kotoba-lang/swift docs/adr/0001-real-wire-format.md"
                          "zero-blast-radius verified before removing old placeholder API: kotoba-lang/kessai was the only other consumer of kotoba.swift in this superproject and only used bic-valid? (unchanged)"
                          "tests 42 -> 207 assertions all green; clj-kondo clean"]
  :adr/supersedes []
