  :adr/decision-summary
  "{:context \"kotoba-lang/swift modeled SWIFT MT + ISO 20022 as plain EDN records (deliberate documented placeholder), incompatible with a real banking backend; cloud-itonami-isic-6493 (factoring actor, concurrent work) and its Cloudflare Worker deployment need standards-accurate banking-message capability to eventually wire into, though no live SWIFTNet/bank connection will ever be attached from this codebase (licensed FI required)\",
    :decision {:mt \"real SWIFT FIN wire format for MT103 (Single Customer Credit Transfer) and MT202 (General Financial Institution Transfer): {1:}{2:}{3:}{4:}{5:} brace blocks, real field tags (20/23B/32A/50K/59/70/71A etc), mt->wire / parse-mt-wire lossless round-trip\"
              :iso20022 \"real XML for pain.001.001.09 (CustomerCreditTransferInitiation) and pacs.008.001.08 (FIToFICustomerCreditTransfer) via new kotoba.swift.iso20022 ns, generated with kotoba-lang/xml (dependency-free Hiccup->XML emitter) + minimal recursive-descent parser scoped to this library's own generated documents\"
              :bic \"ISO 9362 validation unchanged (already correct)\"
              :purity \"no network, no I/O kept -- construction/parsing only\"
              :ui-export \"kotoba.swift.ui / kotoba.swift.export updated to render/export the real wire string and real XML, not the old EDN shape\"},
    :verification-sources [\"iotafinance.com SWIFT ISO15022 MT103/MT202 field-tag detail views (full field lists)\"
                            \"paymentsdomain.com + dev.prowidesoftware.com SWIFT MT block-structure references (Block 1/2 exact layout + worked examples)\"
                            \"swiftmt103.com raw MT103 example (block-3/5 sub-block shape, block-4 -} termination)\"
                            \"knowledge.xmldation.com field-20 T26 usage-rule reference\"
                            \"SWIFT Standards MT Category 1 field-23B references + sepaforcorporates.com/paymentbrief.com field-71A OUR/SHA/BEN explainers\"
                            \"docs.lhv.com pain.001.001.09 format guide + developer.huntington.com pain001 docs\"
                            \"ohmyfin.ai worked pacs.008.001.08 XML example (per-transaction Dbtr/DbtrAgt/CdtrAgt/Cdtr structure, UETR)\"
                            \"knowledge.xmldation.com + mx-message.com ChargeBearerType1Code (DEBT/CRED/SHAR/SLEV) external code list\"],
    :scope-not-covered [\"SWIFT MT: only MT103/MT202; within those, no 13C/23E/26T/36/50A/50F/51A/53a-56a/59A/59F/71F/71G/77B; Block 2 Output direction parsed only as opaque marker, not decoded; Block 5 CHK is opaque, no SWIFT checksum algorithm implemented\"
                         \"ISO 20022: only pain.001.001.09/pacs.008.001.08; within those, no PstlAdr/ultimate debtor-creditor/purpose codes/structured remittance; no camt.05x/pacs.002/004/009; no XSD schema validation, only structural presence checks of modeled elements\"
                         \"no SWIFTNet/bank connection from this codebase, ever -- requires a licensed financial institution downstream\"
                         \"kotoba-lang/kessai's own separate hand-rolled single-transaction pain.001 XML builder (kotoba.kessai.wire/->pain001-xml) left untouched, out of scope for this change\"],
    :landing {:repo-commit \"kotoba-lang/swift main 00b51ce26e58878abff52e0db31bd05eb69c7e55 (server-side merge of feat/real-wire-format, branch deleted)\"
              :tests \"42 -> 207 assertions, all green; clj-kondo 0 errors 0 warnings\"
              :west-pin \"manifest/west.yml swift entry 7290f20... -> 00b51ce... via single-entry GitHub API PUT (blob-SHA optimistic lock, diff limited to one revision: line), commit f99d649df0da28ff2f606c42ed5354ae2f1313b6, verified nbb scripts/gen-west-manifest.cljs --check == up to date from a topdir-isolated sibling worktree (removed after use)\"}}"
  :adr/addendum-2026-07-15-kessai-migration
  {:summary "Migrated the one follow-up this ADR's own Consequences flagged:
             kotoba-lang/kessai's kotoba.kessai.wire/->pain001-xml now
             delegates to kotoba.swift.iso20022/pain001-doc + xml->str
             instead of its own hand-rolled string-splicing builder."
   :gaps-surfaced-and-fixed
   ["<CreDtTm/> and <Dbtr><Nm/></Dbtr> both rendered EMPTY in the old
     hand-rolled builder -- credit-transfer never collected
     creation-date-time or debtor-name at all. pain001-doc correctly
     refuses to build an incomplete document (nil for a missing required
     field), so credit-transfer now requires debtor-name,
     creation-date-time, payment-info-id, and requested-execution-date"
    "amount conversion (major units -> integer minor units, required by
     pain001-doc) introduces a NEW failure mode the old code never had:
     silent sub-cent precision loss (e.g. 12.567 -> 1257). Closed with a
     representable-in-2-decimals? guard that throws instead of silently
     rounding away money -- empirically verified 2.675 is correctly
     rejected (2.675*100 == 267.5 exactly, genuinely not a whole cent)"]
   :blast-radius "confirmed contained to kotoba-lang/kessai alone -- its
                  wire namespace has no external callers; kotoba.kessai's
                  own main namespace only mentions it in docstrings, never
                  requires/calls it"
   :verification
   {:full-suite "clojure -M:test: 10 tests / 87 assertions (was 66), 0
                 failures/errors; clj-kondo 0 errors 0 warnings"
    :test-style "rewritten to use parse-xml/xml-find/xml-text for
                 structural assertions (robust to the real emitter's
                 pretty-printed whitespace) instead of raw string regex
                 assuming compact XML, matching iso20022_test.cljc's own
                 convention"
    :readme-example "updated and independently re-run to confirm it still
                      works end to end"}
   :landed
